WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.506 --> 00:00:01.743
(whooshing noise)

00:00:01.743 --> 00:00:04.243
(ball bounce)

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.029
- [Evan] The extraordinary
way to one million dollars.

00:00:15.029 --> 00:00:17.448
If I'm able to live an extraordinary life,

00:00:17.448 --> 00:00:19.891
If I'm able to do extraordinary things,

00:00:19.891 --> 00:00:21.740
there's a gift in that.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.620
If I'm an extraordinary father,

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.387
that's a gift from my kids.

00:00:25.387 --> 00:00:27.599
If I'm able to run an
extraordinary business,

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:29.154
with extraordinary people,

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:32.340
that's a culture that I'm
able to give my staff.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.090
Mark Drager, CEO of Phanta Media.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.360
Mark Drager didn't want to be ordinary.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.368
After being an entrepreneur for years

00:00:40.368 --> 00:00:42.383
he found himself feeling
more and more like

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:45.185
he wasn't making a
significant contribution

00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:47.094
to his video production company

00:00:47.094 --> 00:00:48.630
Phanta Media.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.599
He had grown his business, hired people

00:00:50.599 --> 00:00:53.098
to do most of the tasks
that he used to do.

00:00:53.098 --> 00:00:56.118
But he wanted to do something meaningful.

00:00:56.118 --> 00:00:57.368
Mark felt lost.

00:00:58.232 --> 00:01:00.954
After about six months of
thinking about his role

00:01:00.954 --> 00:01:04.161
he realized that his motivation
didn't come from money.

00:01:04.161 --> 00:01:05.791
It never did.

00:01:05.791 --> 00:01:07.441
The prospect of making more money

00:01:07.441 --> 00:01:09.611
wouldn't push him to work harder.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:12.851
His motivation comes from
recognition by others.

00:01:12.851 --> 00:01:14.670
He wants to stand out.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.693
He realized that he had a
deep fear of being ordinary

00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:20.009
in all areas of his life.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:22.676
Mark wanted to be extraordinary.

00:01:24.475 --> 00:01:26.587
He wanted to be an extraordinary husband.

00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:28.878
An extraordinary father to his four kids.

00:01:28.878 --> 00:01:30.654
And extraordinary man of faith.

00:01:30.654 --> 00:01:32.999
An extraordinary member of his community.

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:35.965
And, an extraordinary entrepreneur.

00:01:35.965 --> 00:01:38.103
When he was doing something extraordinary

00:01:38.103 --> 00:01:40.159
it made him happy.

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:42.438
That was the connective tissue for him.

00:01:42.438 --> 00:01:45.502
It was missing in his business
which made him feel lost.

00:01:45.502 --> 00:01:47.480
And for him to be happy and successful

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.378
he knew he had to build his business

00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:51.668
around being extraordinary.

00:01:51.668 --> 00:01:53.595
So he changed his company's mission

00:01:53.595 --> 00:01:55.380
to creating extraordinary video

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.746
and aligned his entire business around it.

00:01:58.746 --> 00:02:00.973
He hires extraordinary staff members.

00:02:00.973 --> 00:02:03.196
He works on extraordinary projects.

00:02:03.196 --> 00:02:06.130
He creates extraordinary
results for his clients.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.699
And his team holds him
accountable, as well

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:12.883
to make sure everyone is
given an extraordinary effort.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.450
Focusing on being
extraordinary helped Mark

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.767
pass his million dollar revenue goal

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:20.081
and now he's going for more.

00:02:20.081 --> 00:02:22.676
Finding his one word wasn't
something that came easily

00:02:22.676 --> 00:02:25.147
but by digging deeper into who he was

00:02:25.147 --> 00:02:26.857
it became clear to him

00:02:26.857 --> 00:02:30.159
and it can become clear to you, as well.

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:32.992
(whooshing noise)

00:02:49.876 --> 00:02:51.197
(whooshing noise)

00:02:51.197 --> 00:02:52.311
(ball bounce)

